<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="container hero-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Per-directory model routing · Claude Code + OpenCode · MIT</p>
    <h1>Claude Code. Your models.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      run-claude routes Claude Code — and OpenCode — through a local, self-healing model gateway.
      Map the <code>opus</code> / <code>sonnet</code> / <code>haiku</code> / <code>fable</code>
      tiers onto any provider you bring, per project directory. Your keys, your machine,
      your economics.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="#install">Install from source</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="#tiers">See the tier mappings</a>
    </div>
    <p class="cta-fine"><em>Local-only gateway (127.0.0.1) · BYO API keys · MIT licensed</em></p>

    <figure class="install-block" aria-label="Quick start commands">
      <figcaption class="install-title">Quick start</figcaption>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/noizu/run-claude &amp;&amp; cd run-claude
make install
run-claude secrets init --generate

cd /path/to/my/project
run-claude set-folder groq &amp;&amp; direnv allow
claude</code></pre>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BENEFITS (3-up) -->
<section class="section" id="features">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="visually-hidden">Why run-claude</h2>
    <div class="benefit-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Claude Code, your models</h3>
        <p>
          Keep the Code UX, swap the economics. Directory-scoped profiles map the
          <code>opus</code> / <code>sonnet</code> / <code>haiku</code> / <code>fable</code> tiers
          onto 211 catalogued models across 35 provider profiles. <code>cd</code> into a project
          and that project's models come with it — no flags, no restarts.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Your subscription, where it makes sense</h3>
        <p>
          The <code>claude-plan</code> profile forwards Anthropic requests with your original
          OAuth token — Pro/Max billing, not API billing — while other providers in the same
          profile use their own keys. Blend all of it in one profile.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Local gateway, no middleman</h3>
        <p>
          Front proxy and gateway run on <code>127.0.0.1</code>; your keys stay in
          <code>~/.config/run-claude/.secrets</code>. A watchdog daemon restarts crashed proxies
          (~5s poll), a janitor expires idle models after a 15-minute lease, and the default
          gateway is a single static Go binary.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TIER TABLE -->
<section class="section section-tiers" id="tiers">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Tier mappings are one YAML stanza</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Every profile maps Claude Code's model tiers. User overrides in
      <code>~/.config/run-claude/profiles/</code> win over built-ins; <code>model: null</code>
      disables an entry.
    </p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="tier-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Profile</th>
            <th scope="col">fable</th>
            <th scope="col">opus</th>
            <th scope="col">sonnet</th>
            <th scope="col">haiku</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>anthropic</td>
            <td>claude-fable-5-1</td>
            <td>claude-opus-5</td>
            <td>claude-sonnet-5</td>
            <td>claude-haiku-4-5-20251001</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>claude-plan <span class="tag">OAuth</span></td>
            <td>claude-fable-5-1</td>
            <td>claude-opus-5</td>
            <td>claude-sonnet-5</td>
            <td>claude-haiku-4-5-20251001</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>wafer</td>
            <td>wafer/kimi-k3[1m]</td>
            <td>wafer/glm-5.3-flash (max)[1m]</td>
            <td>wafer/qwen3.5-397b-a17b (high)[1m]</td>
            <td>wafer/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-fast[1m]</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>zai-pro</td>
            <td>zai/glm-5.3 (sub)</td>
            <td>zai/glm-5.3-flash (sub)</td>
            <td>zai/glm-5.3-flash (sub)</td>
            <td>zai/glm-5.3-flash (sub)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>cerebras</td>
            <td>cerebras/zai-glm-4.7</td>
            <td>cerebras/qwen-3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507</td>
            <td>cerebras/gpt-oss-120b</td>
            <td>cerebras/llama-3.3-70b</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>alibaba</td>
            <td>alibaba/deepseek-v4-pro-0813</td>
            <td>alibaba/qwen3.8-max</td>
            <td>alibaba/glm-5.2</td>
            <td>alibaba/qwen3.6-flash</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="table-caption">
      Six of 35 built-in profiles. <code>[1m]</code> marks a 1M-context alias; <code>(sub)</code>
      marks a subscription-key binding. Groq, DeepSeek, OpenAI, Gemini, Grok, Azure, Mistral,
      Perplexity, OpenRouter, and local Ollama/vLLM ship too — or write your own.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
<section class="section" id="how">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Point a directory at a profile</h3>
        <p>
          <code>run-claude set-folder groq &amp;&amp; direnv allow</code>. One <code>.envrc</code>,
          one stable directory token.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Enter the directory</h3>
        <p>
          The shell hook hot-registers the profile's models on the running gateway (refcounted,
          leased, janitored) and swaps auth per provider. Anthropic requests keep your OAuth
          token; everything else uses the gateway master key.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Run <code>claude</code></h3>
        <p>
          Tier env vars are already set, requests flow through <code>127.0.0.1:4443</code>, and
          the CLI sees the live catalog via its bootstrap endpoint. <code>run-claude with groq</code>
          does the same in a one-shot without pinning the directory.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INSTALL -->
<section class="section section-install" id="install">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      run-claude installs from source — clone the repo and <code>make install</code>, which builds
      the <code>go-litellm</code> gateway and then installs the CLI with
      <code>uv tool install .</code>. Packaged installs are planned; for now, this is the way.
    </p>

    <h3 class="install-sub">Prerequisites</h3>
    <ul class="prereq-list">
      <li><strong>Python 3 + uv</strong> — the CLI installs as a uv tool</li>
      <li><strong>Go 1.22+</strong> — builds the default <code>go-litellm</code> gateway binary
        (skipped with a warning if absent)</li>
      <li><strong>Docker</strong> — runs the gateway database container</li>
      <li><strong>direnv</strong> — per-directory activation</li>
      <li><strong>Claude Code and/or the OpenCode CLI</strong> — the agents being routed</li>
    </ul>

    <figure class="install-block" aria-label="Install commands">
      <figcaption class="install-title">From source</figcaption>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/noizu/run-claude &amp;&amp; cd run-claude
make install                        # builds go-litellm gateway, then uv tool install .
run-claude secrets init --generate  # provider API keys + auto-generated DB password

cd /path/to/my/project
run-claude set-folder cerebras      # writes .envrc; prints your stable directory token
direnv allow

claude                              # models registered on entry; just works
run-claude status --health          # verify: proxies, DB, refcounts as JSON</code></pre>
    </figure>
    <p class="table-caption">
      Not on PyPI — install from source as above. Provider keys live in
      <code>~/.config/run-claude/.secrets</code>; never commit that file.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="section section-faq" id="faq">
  <div class="container container-narrow">
    <h2>Questions you'd ask before trusting it</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do my API keys leave my machine?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Keys live in <code>~/.config/run-claude/.secrets</code> and are read by the gateway
          on your localhost. Provider calls go from your machine to the provider — there is no
          hosted relay, no account, and nothing to opt out of.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Does it break Claude Code features?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Code still speaks the Anthropic API it already speaks: the front proxy serves the
          CLI's bootstrap endpoint, pre-registers <code>[1m]</code> 1M-context aliases (39 of
          them) so big-context requests route instead of 404, and a provider-compat callback
          strips fields strict providers reject. Tools, MCP, sessions — unchanged.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Which providers are supported?</summary>
        <p>
          Anthropic, OpenAI, Z.AI, Groq, Cerebras, Wafer, Alibaba (Qwen Token Plan), DeepSeek,
          Gemini, Azure, Grok, Mistral, Perplexity, OpenRouter — plus local Ollama / vLLM /
          LM Studio. 35 built-in profiles, 211 catalogued model definitions.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Where does the configuration live?</summary>
        <p>
          Built-ins ship with the tool. Your overrides in
          <code>~/.config/run-claude/profiles/</code> and
          <code>~/.config/run-claude/models.yaml</code> take priority — same name wins,
          <code>model: null</code> disables and falls through. Per-directory routing is a
          <code>.envrc</code>.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I still use my Claude Pro/Max subscription?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes — that's the <code>claude-plan</code> profile: your original OAuth token is
          forwarded, so subscription billing applies to Claude models while other providers in
          the profile bill their own keys.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What's the license?</summary>
        <p>MIT. Fork it, fork the gateway, ship your own profile pack.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

